WEBVTT

00:00.720 --> 00:03.420
Two cities by the name of Otowa exist:

00:03.420 --> 00:07.040
the real city built upon burned-down bricks,

00:07.040 --> 00:11.970
and the fraudulent city, which has carried the city's image to peaceful, beautiful lands.

00:11.970 --> 00:13.820
It bears a painful past,

00:13.820 --> 00:16.300
and its cornerstone is this misfortune.

00:16.300 --> 00:18.270
As everyday activities are woven,

00:18.270 --> 00:21.860
the city becomes engulfed in the sparkles called human beings.

00:21.860 --> 00:24.230
The real city becomes a shadow of the fake,

00:24.230 --> 00:27.160
while the fake city becomes reality.

00:27.160 --> 00:32.420
What is sought there after time, space, and repeated memories have left it unrecognizable?

00:32.420 --> 00:34.170
That is...

00:53.650 --> 00:59.740
Now that I think about it, that might have been when it all began.

01:00.120 --> 01:02.870
It's dangerous. Don't stand up there!

01:02.870 --> 01:06.870
Oh? You're kind, aren't you, Himura Yu-san?

01:08.730 --> 01:10.420
Who are you?

01:10.420 --> 01:12.420
I'm Yuko.

01:12.420 --> 01:15.010
Yuko?

01:15.660 --> 01:22.180
If... If you've forgotten, please don't say any more.

01:22.180 --> 01:26.420
Please forget this ever happened. This will be farewell.

01:33.030 --> 01:38.990
Himura Yu-san. Even now, I despise you.

01:43.540 --> 01:44.870
Yo, Himura.

01:44.870 --> 01:46.700
Is this all right, Kuze?

01:46.700 --> 01:49.440
The weather is chilly around this time, so it's fine.

01:49.440 --> 01:50.630
Where's the princess?

01:50.630 --> 01:53.460
She went to sleep long ago. And you?

01:53.460 --> 01:58.210
The same as you. Are you reminiscing about the past again?

01:58.210 --> 02:01.650
Heh, who knows? I've forgotten the past.

02:01.650 --> 02:05.270
I'll go greet the girl myself next time.

02:06.060 --> 02:08.640
Heh, what a joke.

02:11.010 --> 02:14.440
Himura, will you stick around for the recital tomorrow?

02:14.440 --> 02:15.450
Recital?

02:15.450 --> 02:18.760
Yeah. A recital for you and your girl.

02:18.760 --> 02:21.570
That's all. Nothing else.

02:21.570 --> 02:22.950
Ah, a <i>fermata.</i>

02:21.570 --> 02:24.200
Fermata: musical notation for a sustained or stretched note.
Fine: musical notation for the end of a repeated segment.

02:22.950 --> 02:24.200
No, it's a <i>fine.</i>

02:24.200 --> 02:26.500
But if it's an exhibition, wouldn't it be a <i>fermata?</i>

02:26.500 --> 02:27.940
You seem to know your stuff.

02:27.940 --> 02:29.990
You're the one who told me.

02:29.990 --> 02:32.960
Oh, I might have.

02:32.960 --> 02:35.990
Hmm, would it be a <i>fermata?</i>

02:35.990 --> 02:38.260
For my current situation, it would clearly be...

02:41.060 --> 02:44.350
Oh yeah, a girl is visiting Renji's house.

02:44.350 --> 02:45.780
A girl?

02:45.780 --> 02:47.010
You didn't know?

02:47.010 --> 02:49.950
I haven't really seen him in a while.

02:49.950 --> 02:51.400
He's your next-door neighbor.

02:51.400 --> 02:54.180
Physical proximity doesn't mean much.

02:54.180 --> 02:59.880
If a girl sits next to you, it doesn't mean you're closer to her than to a girl in another class, right?

02:59.880 --> 03:02.830
Isn't it a problem if you're dating both of them?

03:02.830 --> 03:05.240
It's okay as long as it's not just two.

03:06.580 --> 03:07.450
Huh?

03:07.450 --> 03:09.980
If you're dating two girls, it's a fight.

03:09.980 --> 03:12.400
If you're dating twenty, it's a competition.

03:12.400 --> 03:16.880
When it gets to that point, the girls direct their anger towards each other, not me.

03:16.880 --> 03:18.430
You're an ass.

03:18.430 --> 03:21.880
Girls sometimes develop friendly ties from rivalries, you know.

03:21.880 --> 03:23.430
It's not all that bad.

03:23.430 --> 03:27.480
Now you're a bigger ass for using such a lame excuse.

03:27.480 --> 03:31.640
But they all love me.

03:31.640 --> 03:33.770
Heh. You haven't changed at all.

03:33.770 --> 03:37.900
Of course I haven't. Humans don't change that easily.

03:37.900 --> 03:40.810
Himura, you haven't either, have you?

03:40.810 --> 03:41.700
You've always...

03:42.570 --> 03:43.820
You're right.

03:43.820 --> 03:47.700
Perhaps I haven't changed since that day.

03:47.700 --> 03:49.200
Art Room

03:47.700 --> 03:49.200
Hirono

03:52.160 --> 03:53.420
That idiot.

03:55.830 --> 03:57.340
Yo, Himura.

03:57.340 --> 03:58.930
You workin' today?

03:58.930 --> 03:59.800
Yeah.

03:59.800 --> 04:02.970
Give me a hand, though, before you head off to work?

04:02.970 --> 04:04.840
I'm going to open a flea market.

04:04.840 --> 04:06.550
A flea market?

04:06.550 --> 04:10.930
I was thinking of getting rid of my junk before I left Japan.

04:10.930 --> 04:13.310
Sorry, something just came up.

04:13.310 --> 04:14.620
Something, eh?

04:14.620 --> 04:16.940
If it's a girl, I'll let you go.

04:18.230 --> 04:21.850
It <i>is about a girl, but it's just her.</i>

04:21.850 --> 04:23.990
Please, go right ahead.

04:28.620 --> 04:30.450
Ah, Himura-kun.

04:30.450 --> 04:32.120
Do you have business in the Art Room?

04:33.250 --> 04:35.180
Amamiya-sensei...

04:35.180 --> 04:36.880
This place is non-smoking, you know.

04:37.880 --> 04:40.750
Where there isn't fire, there isn't smoke.

04:40.750 --> 04:43.590
Well then, why do you have it in your mouth?

04:43.590 --> 04:47.550
When people have desires, they want to satisfy them, even if it means using a substitute.

04:47.550 --> 04:51.390
Anyway, you've finally decided to join the Art Club?

04:51.390 --> 04:54.350
I'm glad. All those attempts to convince you weren't a waste.

04:54.350 --> 04:58.150
Nope, I don't plan on joining any clubs.

04:58.150 --> 05:00.200
Don't say things like that.

05:00.200 --> 05:03.530
You've got talent. Letting it deteriorate is such a shame.

05:03.530 --> 05:07.640
I keep telling you, I'm not interested in drawing.

05:07.640 --> 05:09.530
Anyway, I'm in a hurry.

05:09.530 --> 05:11.080
Hirono-san, eh?

05:11.080 --> 05:12.210
Yeah.

05:12.210 --> 05:15.580
It's a hassle, isn't it? Art is such a hassle.

05:15.580 --> 05:18.990
People who venture into the world of art, and those who associate with them,

05:18.990 --> 05:21.030
are all pulled in without realizing it.

05:21.030 --> 05:25.260
So, Himura-kun, you should pull others in. It'd be a lot easier on you.

05:26.050 --> 05:27.510
No, thanks.

05:33.390 --> 05:34.350
Hey.

05:34.350 --> 05:36.180
What the heck are you doing?

05:36.180 --> 05:38.010
You're late, Yu.

05:38.010 --> 05:41.560
I got tired of waiting, so I started drawing.

05:41.560 --> 05:44.400
Sorry, but could you wait a while?

05:44.400 --> 05:46.920
I want to draw until I get to a good stopping point.

05:46.920 --> 05:49.580
You don't have to be naked to draw!

05:49.580 --> 05:50.550
Put on some clothes!

05:50.550 --> 05:51.790
Don't talk nonsense.

05:51.790 --> 05:53.830
I'm drawing a rough draft!

05:53.830 --> 05:56.660
A rough draft doesn't mean drawing in the rough!

05:56.660 --> 05:58.330
It's just an initial sketch!

05:59.040 --> 06:00.500
This is a miracle.

06:00.500 --> 06:03.240
That's the first time I've ever heard you crack a joke.

06:03.240 --> 06:04.630
It wasn't a joke.

06:04.630 --> 06:06.170
Hurry up and put your uniform on!

06:06.170 --> 06:09.430
Sheesh, you're so dull.

06:09.430 --> 06:10.970
Shut up!

06:10.970 --> 06:16.060
You might not know this, but a rough draft is one of the most basic procedures in drawing.

06:16.060 --> 06:19.480
Where else would you find someone dumb enough to be their own model?

06:19.480 --> 06:22.400
A self-portrait is also one of the most basic procedures.

06:22.400 --> 06:26.570
I've never seen a <i>rough self-portrait by van Gogh or Picasso before.</i>

06:28.150 --> 06:30.220
Van Gogh and Picasso were both men.

06:30.220 --> 06:32.820
Even if they <i>did draw themselves, it wouldn't be "rough".</i>

06:32.820 --> 06:34.200
You're stupid, aren't you?

06:35.210 --> 06:37.250
First Kuze, then you.

06:37.250 --> 06:40.330
I honestly can't comprehend the mindset of people who involve themselves with art.

06:40.330 --> 06:43.880
You're not winning any points by equating me to Kuze.

06:43.880 --> 06:45.250
Well,

06:45.250 --> 06:48.160
it might actually be easier to get others involved in art.

06:48.160 --> 06:49.760
What?

06:54.970 --> 06:57.720
If I've got this much, it'll last for a long time.

06:57.720 --> 07:01.780
When are you going to learn how to go shopping by yourself?

07:01.780 --> 07:03.900
There's no point in asking me.

07:03.900 --> 07:05.820
Then who am I supposed to ask?

07:05.820 --> 07:10.770
If you ask me, I find it strange that anyone can walk into a shop alone and buy something.

07:10.770 --> 07:12.430
Yu, you're like that too,

07:12.430 --> 07:14.490
but what's wrong with those people?

07:14.490 --> 07:16.580
<i>You're the one with the problem.</i>

07:17.830 --> 07:19.120
Oh, yeah.

07:19.120 --> 07:21.750
I owe you for coming with me.

07:23.030 --> 07:24.750
You can have this.

07:24.750 --> 07:26.510
I don't want it.

07:26.510 --> 07:28.460
They gave it to me for free.

07:28.460 --> 07:29.640
No need to be considerate.

07:29.640 --> 07:32.220
I'm not. I just don't want it, that's all.

07:32.220 --> 07:34.640
You're such a jerk.

07:35.090 --> 07:38.660
You saw me naked, and yet you can't pay me back?

07:38.660 --> 07:40.480
You have crazy logic.

07:40.480 --> 07:41.810
<i>You're the one who owes <i>me,</i></i>

07:41.810 --> 07:44.020
and you got naked of your own free will!

07:44.020 --> 07:46.230
All the guys wanted to see that.

07:46.230 --> 07:47.190
Who, exactly?

07:48.270 --> 07:52.780
Anyway, Yu. Did you do something that would piss people off?

07:52.780 --> 07:53.740
Huh?

07:53.740 --> 07:56.290
Someone's been following you

07:56.290 --> 07:58.620
ever since we left school.

07:59.240 --> 08:00.750
Hello.

08:00.750 --> 08:01.830
So, who are you?

08:01.830 --> 08:04.880
My name is Amamiya Yuko, a freshman.

08:04.880 --> 08:06.200
An acquaintance of yours?

08:06.200 --> 08:07.250
Nope.

08:07.250 --> 08:09.910
I know him, but he doesn't know me.

08:09.910 --> 08:13.420
That's because Himura-senpai doesn't remember me.

08:19.810 --> 08:20.810
I'm going home.

08:21.770 --> 08:24.000
Nagi? Hey, what's up—

08:24.770 --> 08:27.020
What the hell?

08:32.610 --> 08:34.320
She's really cute.

08:34.320 --> 08:35.490
In what way?

08:35.490 --> 08:37.200
She's so contrary.

08:42.160 --> 08:44.490
She's an honest, strong-willed woman.

08:44.490 --> 08:45.790
I admire her.

08:45.790 --> 08:47.410
Are you two dating?

08:47.410 --> 08:48.810
As if.

08:48.810 --> 08:51.420
She just drags me around.

08:51.420 --> 08:53.250
You haven't changed at all.

08:53.250 --> 08:55.470
You and your prickly attitude.

08:55.470 --> 08:56.370
But...

08:56.370 --> 08:59.520
you don't remember any longer, do you?

09:05.100 --> 09:07.600
Nope, I remember.

09:11.610 --> 09:13.040
I remember now.

09:13.040 --> 09:14.240
Everything.

09:14.240 --> 09:15.670
I see.

09:15.670 --> 09:18.060
It's been a long time, Yuko.

09:18.060 --> 09:20.510
It has, Yu-kun.

09:20.510 --> 09:21.870
Have you been well?

09:21.870 --> 09:25.380
Yes. I'm glad to see that you're doing fine as well.

09:25.380 --> 09:27.320
It's been ten years since then, yes?

09:27.320 --> 09:28.880
Time flies.

09:28.880 --> 09:32.500
For me, it was a long ten years.

09:32.500 --> 09:34.350
What are you doing now?

09:34.350 --> 09:37.310
I'm living with my new brother. It's just the two of us.

09:37.310 --> 09:38.640
I see.

09:38.640 --> 09:40.060
But I'm glad.

09:40.060 --> 09:42.430
I got to meet my onii-chan again.

09:42.430 --> 09:43.390
Stop it.

09:45.310 --> 09:47.090
Don't call me onii-chan.

09:47.090 --> 09:49.050
Right.

09:49.050 --> 09:51.080
We're not in the past anymore.

09:51.080 --> 09:53.000
What do you mean?

09:53.000 --> 09:55.990
I'll be blunt. Don't try to get close to me.

09:58.740 --> 10:01.990
Don't make me remember the past.

10:02.740 --> 10:05.510
Love, I've got to feel it

10:05.790 --> 10:08.790
If you put your trust in me

10:09.110 --> 10:12.360
I know what my life would be

10:12.430 --> 10:17.250
Oh, you are all I ever need

10:17.410 --> 10:22.950
I try to hear what you say

10:23.310 --> 10:25.220
So I pray

10:25.300 --> 10:28.800
But you're fading away

10:30.240 --> 10:35.960
Don't go and break my fragile heart

10:36.390 --> 10:39.590
We won't fall apart

10:39.710 --> 10:47.770
'Cause you're my only star

10:49.730 --> 10:53.480
I wonder why my tears come at night

10:53.480 --> 10:56.990
Calling you, so like a little child

10:57.150 --> 11:00.260
All the things you have in mind

11:00.490 --> 11:03.760
I wish I could see your insides

11:03.760 --> 11:06.890
My love, you've got to feel it

11:06.890 --> 11:09.950
And if we put our trust in you and me

11:10.160 --> 11:13.610
You know what our lives would be

11:13.730 --> 11:21.570
Oh, you are the one, I believe

11:31.960 --> 11:35.500
The distant sky beyond the window
Watching the unreachable clouds

11:48.180 --> 11:49.310
Miki...

11:49.310 --> 11:50.230
Miki!

11:51.890 --> 11:53.060
Mi... ki...

11:53.060 --> 11:55.230
Mizuki!

11:55.230 --> 11:56.730
Mizuki!

11:56.730 --> 11:59.940
Mizuki, it's time for breakfast.

11:59.940 --> 12:01.240
Hmm.

12:02.610 --> 12:03.910
Are you awake now?

12:03.910 --> 12:04.990
Probably.

12:04.990 --> 12:06.030
Probably?

12:06.030 --> 12:07.330
Where is this?

12:07.330 --> 12:08.490
Australia.

12:08.490 --> 12:09.490
Huh?

12:09.490 --> 12:11.120
Why is Renji here?

12:11.120 --> 12:14.630
What do you mean, why? You're the one staying in <i>my house.</i>

12:14.630 --> 12:15.540
How come?

12:15.540 --> 12:19.710
How come? You said you were bored after your school selected you for admission.

12:19.710 --> 12:21.340
You're here to play, aren't you?

12:21.340 --> 12:23.970
Ah, I do remember something like that.

12:23.970 --> 12:25.800
Maybe you're not fully awake yet?

12:27.680 --> 12:29.770
So, why is Renji here?

12:29.770 --> 12:32.310
Like I said, you're the one who—

12:32.310 --> 12:33.390
Oh my, oh my!

12:33.390 --> 12:35.650
You two are so close!

12:36.650 --> 12:39.480
I might tell Chihiro-chan about this!

12:39.480 --> 12:41.030
N-No!

12:41.030 --> 12:42.570
It's not what you think!

12:43.530 --> 12:45.570
I made Spanish omelets for breakfast.

12:45.570 --> 12:47.030
Hurry up, all right?

12:47.030 --> 12:48.160
Okay!

12:48.910 --> 12:52.620
And why am I holding your arm?

12:52.620 --> 12:54.540
I don't know!

12:54.540 --> 12:56.380
Were you having a nightmare or something?

12:57.130 --> 12:59.040
You looked like something was bothering you.

12:59.040 --> 13:01.000
You were reaching out as if you were asking for help.

13:04.840 --> 13:06.130
Anyway!

13:06.130 --> 13:10.010
Renji, do you intend to stick around and stare at my wonderful body while I change?

13:10.010 --> 13:10.760
Eh?

13:10.760 --> 13:12.390
H-Hold on!

13:14.480 --> 13:15.600
Every night.

13:15.600 --> 13:17.020
Hmm?

13:17.020 --> 13:19.190
I have the same dream every night.

13:19.190 --> 13:20.320
The same dream?

13:20.320 --> 13:21.230
Yeah.

13:21.230 --> 13:23.030
A dream about beautiful flowers.

13:23.030 --> 13:25.030
Dream

13:25.360 --> 13:26.450
A violin?

13:26.450 --> 13:28.120
Yeah, a violin.

13:28.120 --> 13:32.830
When I was walking near the church yesterday, I heard a really pretty sound!

13:32.830 --> 13:37.580
The melody that flowed across the sunset was almost like a sea made of music,

13:37.580 --> 13:39.580
and it was marvelous!

13:39.580 --> 13:41.710
That was probably Kuze-san.

13:41.710 --> 13:42.880
Kuze-san?

13:42.880 --> 13:44.760
He's our next-door neighbor.

13:44.760 --> 13:47.050
He's also a world-class violinist.

13:47.050 --> 13:48.220
Wow.

13:48.220 --> 13:51.390
I see. So Kuze-san was playing his violin.

13:51.390 --> 13:53.180
It was so pretty.

13:53.180 --> 13:56.520
Kuze-san occasionally lets us hear him play,

13:56.520 --> 13:59.770
which is so much better than a CD or something like that.

13:59.770 --> 14:00.810
Hey, Renji.

14:00.810 --> 14:02.190
Do you want to introduce him to me?

14:02.190 --> 14:04.780
Introduce you to... who?

14:04.780 --> 14:05.820
Who?

14:05.820 --> 14:07.650
Kuze-san, of course!

14:08.660 --> 14:10.200
Okay? You don't mind, do you?

14:10.200 --> 14:12.910
Well, Kuze-san is a bit...

14:12.910 --> 14:14.750
Is there a problem?

14:14.750 --> 14:18.500
I wouldn't call it a problem, but, ah...

14:18.500 --> 14:22.090
Yeah! Kuze-san is a serious womanizer!

14:22.250 --> 14:22.840
Huh?

14:22.840 --> 14:26.170
He's a little strange, a total weirdo!

14:26.170 --> 14:28.010
I wouldn't recommend it.

14:28.880 --> 14:30.760
I don't need to hear that!

14:30.760 --> 14:33.680
It's not like I'm asking you to find me a boyfriend!

14:33.680 --> 14:36.810
It doesn't matter if he's a weirdo or a womanizer, right?

14:37.810 --> 14:39.480
Really, you're so rude!

14:39.480 --> 14:41.860
I only have eyes for Kei-senpai!

14:41.860 --> 14:46.230
Even if a handsome guy tries to hit on me, I'm not going to fall for it!

14:46.230 --> 14:47.820
But...

14:47.820 --> 14:51.620
In that case, will <i>you keep me company for the rest of the break?</i>

14:51.620 --> 14:55.580
I-I won't be able to! I'm studying for my exams right now.

14:55.580 --> 14:59.410
Isn't that your fault for not studying ahead of time, Renji?

14:59.410 --> 15:01.500
Even if you say that...

15:01.500 --> 15:03.090
Right, Mom?

15:03.090 --> 15:04.920
Hmm, well...

15:04.920 --> 15:06.630
Perhaps we can introduce her?

15:06.630 --> 15:08.010
Really?

15:08.010 --> 15:09.470
Mom!

15:09.470 --> 15:13.550
Kuze-san might have some plans of his own, so we'll ask him first!

15:13.550 --> 15:15.560
Courage

15:17.680 --> 15:19.560
He doesn't seem to be at home.

15:19.560 --> 15:21.440
That's strange...

15:21.440 --> 15:23.810
This is Asou Sumire, your next-door neighbor!

15:23.810 --> 15:26.320
Isn't Kuze-san home?

15:26.320 --> 15:30.320
I wanted to chat, but I guess I'll save it for another time!

15:32.820 --> 15:35.530
Good morning, Sumire-san.

15:35.530 --> 15:37.410
Good morning.

15:37.410 --> 15:40.160
Kuze-san, do you have some time?

15:40.160 --> 15:43.040
Is this perhaps an invitation for a night out?

15:43.040 --> 15:47.090
Well, something similar. It's about deepening relationships.

15:47.090 --> 15:50.880
Have I ever refused an invitation from you?

15:50.880 --> 15:54.970
Ugh... This person really might be a womanizer.

15:54.970 --> 15:57.640
Hmm? Who's this young lady?

15:58.270 --> 15:59.640
Nice to meet you!

15:59.640 --> 16:02.640
My name is Hayama Mizuki!

16:02.640 --> 16:03.150
Mi-

16:03.150 --> 16:03.650
zu-

16:03.650 --> 16:04.150
ki!

16:04.150 --> 16:05.900
All written in katakana!

16:04.150 --> 16:08.900
Katakana is a form of Japanese alphabet, not commonly used for names.

16:05.900 --> 16:07.610
She's my niece.

16:07.610 --> 16:08.860
I see.

16:08.860 --> 16:11.820
Nice to meet you. I'm Kuze Shuichi.

16:14.280 --> 16:15.570
I'm Mizuki!

16:21.080 --> 16:26.210
Renji has his studies, and I've been busy with all of my short-notice work.

16:26.210 --> 16:29.500
Oh, I see. Well, in that case, I don't mind at all.

16:29.500 --> 16:34.010
What a relief! Then you don't mind keeping Mizuki-chan company?

16:34.010 --> 16:36.890
Of course not! If you want me to, I'd be happy to please.

16:36.890 --> 16:39.060
Are you happy, Mizuki-chan?

16:39.060 --> 16:40.100
Yes!

16:40.100 --> 16:41.310
I'll be in your care!

16:41.310 --> 16:43.350
No, no. The pleasure is all mine.

16:43.350 --> 16:47.060
It's flattering that I get to keep such a beautiful young lady company.

16:47.060 --> 16:49.400
A beautiful young lady?

16:49.400 --> 16:52.400
You're always helping me out, Sumire-san.

16:52.400 --> 16:57.530
If there's anything I can do, I'd like to repay those favors as soon as possible.

16:57.530 --> 16:59.530
As soon as possible?

16:59.530 --> 17:00.490
That's...

17:00.490 --> 17:02.000
Oh, I'm sorry.

17:02.000 --> 17:04.620
I shouldn't have said that.

17:04.620 --> 17:06.370
Forget I said anything.

17:06.370 --> 17:07.330
Okay.

17:13.340 --> 17:16.550
Kuze-san, did you move in here recently?

17:16.550 --> 17:19.430
I've been here for a while. Why do you ask?

17:19.430 --> 17:21.220
You don't seem to own a lot of furniture.

17:21.220 --> 17:23.980
Ah. I've gotten rid of a lot of things.

17:23.980 --> 17:24.980
You have?

17:24.980 --> 17:26.600
Yeah, depending on my mood.

17:26.600 --> 17:29.440
You get rid of your furniture depending on your mood?

17:29.440 --> 17:32.610
Yeah. Furniture, clothes, everything.

17:32.610 --> 17:34.030
Isn't it nice and roomy in here?

17:34.030 --> 17:35.700
Yeah, I guess.

17:35.700 --> 17:38.530
He does seem a little unusual.

17:38.530 --> 17:39.320
This place...

17:39.950 --> 17:43.080
You can come whenever you want, and use it for whatever you want.

17:43.080 --> 17:44.370
Really?

17:44.370 --> 17:48.630
Yeah. I have a lot of unused rooms,
and it's too big for me to live in alone.

17:48.630 --> 17:50.920
Ah! Thank you so much!

17:50.920 --> 17:55.920
I have my own room, but I couldn't throw away my favorite manga,

17:55.920 --> 17:58.470
so now there's just too much stuff.

17:59.720 --> 18:02.060
I've always admired such a large room.

18:02.560 --> 18:03.970
Ah! That place is—

18:05.390 --> 18:06.480
This is...

18:06.480 --> 18:11.480
Well, to clear up any misunderstandings, those aren't intended for me to wear.

18:11.480 --> 18:14.190
Anyway, I'll probably get rid of them as well.

18:14.190 --> 18:15.650
These too?

18:15.650 --> 18:16.530
Yeah.

18:17.200 --> 18:19.910
No, you can't throw them away.

18:19.910 --> 18:21.910
Eyes

18:24.660 --> 18:30.290
Heh, if you got in, you must be pretty smart, right?

18:30.290 --> 18:34.800
Not really. I studied hard because I wanted to get into Otowa.

18:38.340 --> 18:40.470
That's a violin, isn't it?

18:40.470 --> 18:42.100
Ah, yeah it is.

18:43.140 --> 18:46.520
Kuze-san, I've got a little favor to ask of you.

18:46.520 --> 18:47.730
What is it?

18:47.730 --> 18:50.980
Would you mind playing it a little?

18:52.400 --> 18:55.690
You're a professional, aren't you?

18:55.690 --> 18:58.150
I really want to hear a live performance!

19:03.660 --> 19:04.950
Kuze-san?

19:04.950 --> 19:06.410
Ah, sorry about that.

19:06.410 --> 19:08.460
To tell you the truth, I can't play it right now.

19:08.460 --> 19:10.080
That thing's broken.

19:10.080 --> 19:11.500
Eh?

19:11.500 --> 19:14.340
Sorry to disappoint you.

19:14.340 --> 19:16.460
Aw, I'm so disappointed.

19:16.460 --> 19:19.220
I was hoping to hear you play.

19:19.220 --> 19:21.510
I wanted a raw live performance!

19:21.510 --> 19:23.720
I like it better raw, too.

19:23.720 --> 19:24.720
Without a condom.

19:24.720 --> 19:25.640
Huh?

19:25.640 --> 19:28.140
Maybe next time.

19:28.140 --> 19:29.520
Yeah!

19:30.310 --> 19:31.140
Oh, yeah.

19:31.140 --> 19:32.900
If you don't mind, I've got some albums.

19:33.900 --> 19:36.860
Hmm, this one might be good.

19:37.280 --> 19:38.530
Ah!

19:38.530 --> 19:40.530
You're really on the cover, Kuze-san!

19:40.530 --> 19:42.110
Trying to look cool, too!

19:42.110 --> 19:43.410
And you look so young!

19:43.410 --> 19:44.990
If you want it, you can have it.

19:44.990 --> 19:46.530
Thanks so much!

19:50.540 --> 19:51.870
What's up?

19:51.870 --> 19:53.540
My stomach's calling.

19:53.540 --> 19:55.500
Mizuki-chan, would you like something to drink?

19:55.500 --> 19:58.300
Yes, please!

19:58.300 --> 20:01.220
I have plenty, so take what you'd like.

20:01.220 --> 20:02.550
Okay!

20:04.590 --> 20:08.640
This fridge only has alcohol and juice?

20:08.640 --> 20:10.230
That's not true.

20:11.640 --> 20:13.400
See? I've got ice too.

20:24.820 --> 20:27.660
I've been living for this one cup!

20:28.990 --> 20:32.870
But this room is really beautiful, isn't it?

20:32.870 --> 20:33.920
Beautiful?

20:33.920 --> 20:37.500
Yeah! It looks like I could lie around from corner to corner!

20:37.500 --> 20:38.750
Lie around?

20:38.750 --> 20:40.840
Yes! Lie around!

20:46.430 --> 20:48.050
Ah!

20:48.050 --> 20:50.560
This feels nice!

20:50.560 --> 20:52.180
You're right.

20:52.180 --> 20:56.100
Even if you lounge around my house, you'll never get a view like this.

20:56.100 --> 20:58.150
Furniture, manga, and more manga.

20:58.150 --> 20:59.610
There's just too much stuff.

20:59.610 --> 21:01.320
Heh, I see.

21:03.570 --> 21:06.200
I guess having nothing around can be beautiful.

21:06.200 --> 21:06.950
Eh?

21:06.950 --> 21:09.780
I don't have any classes, homework,

21:09.780 --> 21:12.540
or anything else I have to do.

21:17.540 --> 21:23.050
It's a pleasure to do nothing at all in a place where nothing exists.

21:24.970 --> 21:27.300
I want to lie around forever!

21:27.300 --> 21:31.850
If I ever lie around, it's for really stupid reasons.

21:31.850 --> 21:33.600
You referred to yourself as "ore" again.

21:33.600 --> 21:34.520
Hmm?

21:34.520 --> 21:37.520
You call yourself "ore" and "watashi".

21:34.520 --> 21:40.110
"Ore" and "watashi" are both ways of referring to oneself. "Ore" is more casual, "watashi" more formal.

21:37.520 --> 21:40.110
There's no need to hold back. You can be natural!

21:40.110 --> 21:41.650
I'm not holding back.

21:41.650 --> 21:45.320
When I'm working, I have to interact with uptight people,

21:45.320 --> 21:47.780
TPO is a Japanese pseudo-Anglicism meaning "time, place, occasion".

21:45.320 --> 21:47.780
and I switch back and forth, depending on the TPO.

21:47.780 --> 21:50.450
Well then, could you switch out of work mode?

21:50.450 --> 21:53.290
I'm tired of speaking elegantly.

21:53.290 --> 21:55.160
You too?

21:56.160 --> 22:00.420
Girls are always feigning innocence.

22:03.210 --> 22:06.670
Yeah, this is easier for me as well.

22:06.670 --> 22:08.510
Hah, it's like a switch!

22:08.510 --> 22:13.720
When you get to my age, what used to be a mask eventually becomes a part of you.

22:13.720 --> 22:14.810
A mask?

22:14.810 --> 22:18.690
Humans have many masks.

22:18.690 --> 22:21.190
As you age and form more relationships with other people,

22:21.190 --> 22:23.070
the number of masks you have increases.

22:24.480 --> 22:28.240
Well, that's just one of life's many little toppings.

22:28.240 --> 22:29.570
I see...

22:29.570 --> 22:33.990
Well, if you're going to wear a mask, cat ears are a lot cuter!

22:33.990 --> 22:36.660
Isn't it kinda gross if a guy wears them?

22:36.660 --> 22:38.000
Maybe.

22:40.960 --> 22:44.250
But I think that you look a lot better without a mask.

22:44.250 --> 22:45.510
Eh?

22:45.510 --> 22:46.210
Yeah.

22:46.210 --> 22:49.590
When you're talking with me, I'd like to hear your normal voice.

22:53.220 --> 22:55.720
It was fun talking to you today!

22:55.720 --> 22:57.230
Well, I'm glad.

22:57.230 --> 22:59.480
Well then, see you tomorrow.

23:02.440 --> 23:04.020
See you tomorrow.

23:04.900 --> 23:10.910
With a laughter on the way home

23:04.900 --> 23:10.910
My searching for sometimes lost voice

23:15.160 --> 23:17.250
A mask, huh.

23:28.130 --> 23:31.680
<i>Fermata... Sustain it longer...</i>

23:31.680 --> 23:35.010
Longer, until when?

23:37.020 --> 23:39.480
An overture of a meeting and a reunion.

23:39.480 --> 23:41.520
ef - a tale of melodies.

23:41.520 --> 23:42.770
Read.

23:42.770 --> 23:45.940
Can you hear it? The melody of truth.
